From 09ebe427a48f437713727252f0acd70bbb190244 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 08:19:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 118/127] media: sprd: add an SC7730 VSP userspace bridge

Provide the SCX35 VSP register and interrupt ABI for local decoder
bring-up on SC7730. Retain vendor ioctl numbers, including pointer
arguments on commands historically encoded as _IO. Serialize engine
ownership and bound register mappings, allocation sizes and IRQ waits.

Keep MM runtime power and clocks pinned by each open file, including
register VMAs, and block system suspend while raw mappings may be used.
Only access VSP registers after genpd powers the MM domain. Expose the
raw DMA interface as root-only with CAP_SYS_RAWIO, and add a local ioctl
for file-owned coherent CMA buffers.

Move shared MM AHB gates and resets to a syscon regmap used by DCAM and
VSP, avoiding independent read-modify-write races. Drop only VSP-private
gates on runtime suspend; DCAM retains its MM genpd reference.

Enable VSP on gtelwifi with SPI 43 and the vendor clock mux levels.
Add bindings for the VSP and shared MM AHB block. This is a bring-up
bridge, not a registered V4L2 or Codec2 decoder; actual hardware decode
and concurrent camera operation still require device validation.

Assisted-by: GPT-6 (Codex)
